{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|Canada|US|alone|or|postpositive|chiefly|humorous}} Of a [[fact#Noun|fact]], [[subject#Noun|subject]], etc.: [[basic#Adjective|basic]], [[beginner]]-[[level#Noun|level]], [[elementary#Adjective|elementary]].
#: {{ux|en|Geology '''101''' tells us that you can’t build a reservoir on sandstone.}}
#: {{ux|en|My dog flunked out of Crate Training '''101'''.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year='''1964''' March (date recorded)|speaker=w:Woody Allen|title=Private Life|album=[[w:Woody Allen (album)|Woody Allen]]|series=CP 518|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250117203546/http://www.ibras.dk/comedy/allen.htm#Private|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Colpix Records|year_published=July 1964|oclc=15860789|passage=I went to NYU myself, I was a philo-major there, too. I took all the abstract philosophy courses in college, like truth and beauty, advanced truth and beauty, intermediate truth, introduction to God, Death '''101'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Time|date=6 November 1972|author=[[w:Gerald Clarke (author)|Gerald Clarke]]|title=Show Business: Viewpoints: {{w|The Rookies}}. ABC. Monday, 8–9 p.m. E.S.T.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20110129051600/http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,942627,00.html|passage=Since this is a series that emphasizes Social Relevance '''101'''—a basic course on TV these days—the hood in that episode is just a good ghetto boy who has been led astray, and the cop is good old Paddy on the beat.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=w:Daniel Dor|chapter=When Relativism Becomes a Marketing Strategy: Globalization, Knowledge and the World Language System|series=CPS Books|editor=Andrea Krizsán; Violetta Zentai|title=Reshaping Globalization: Multilateral Dialogues and New Policy Initiatives|location=Budapest, Hungary&#59; New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:CEU Press|Central European University Press]]|section=part I (Production of Global Knowledge)|page=66|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/reshapingglobali0000unse/page/66/mode/1up|isbn=978-963-9241-63-3|issn=1587-6942|passage=Companies sell directories, databases, reports, translation services, automatic translation software—and guidebooks for doing business away from home, which, in some cases, look much like simplified textbooks for Anthropology '''101'''.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|date=22 June 2003|writers=Holly Henderson; w:Liz Tigelaar|actor=w:Jennifer Hale|role=Samantha (“Sam”)|episode=Ski Trip|title=w:Totally Spies!|season=2|number=21|network=w:Teletoon|location=Montreal, Que.|publisher=w:Marathon Media|oclc=811406458|passage=Ugh! Crash and burn! Next year, I’m taking flirting '''101'''! I am so not good at this!}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=1 November 2009|author=w:Bob Schieffer|title=Face the Nation: A Class in Nation-building 101|work=w:CBS News|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250124002343/https://www.cbsnews.com/news/a-class-in-nation-building-101/|passage=A Class in Nation-Building '''101''' {{quote-gloss|title}} As the President tries to develop a new strategy in Afghanistan, I wonder if this is the real lesson that we've learned in Afghanistan so far: that nation-building, like charity, probably begins at home.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|date=12 September 2017|speaker=w:Norm Macdonald|title=w:Norm Macdonald Live|season=3|number=11|passage=I'm taking a fascinating class all about the {{w|Hollywood Freeway}}. It's called 101: '''101'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=20 March 2023|author=Rebecca Gillam; Bridie Wilkins|title={{w|Alexandra Daddario}} and Her PT on How She Built Her Baywatch Bod + Her 10 Regular Workout Rules|editor=Liz Plosser|journal=[[w:Women's Health (magazine)|Women’s Health]]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230621161528/https://www.womenshealthmag.com/uk/fitness/a39462034/alexandra-daddario-workout/|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Hearst Communications|Hearst Magazine Media]]|issn=0884-7355|oclc=1102801076|passage=However much you work out, but especially if it's a lot, learning correct form and focusing on keeping your body safe is '''101'''—not just while exercising, but also how you move around day to day.}}

=====Usage notes=====
The word is used humorously or sarcastically with subjects, etc., that would usually never form the title of actual college courses.

